# Volt reference redesign — 2026-10-30

The Electric car's procedural body, cabin and details were rebuilt around the supplied silver fastback reference. The body has a shorter bonnet, closed front, shallow door sculpt, fitted rear deck and slim lights. Separate windscreen, roof, rear screen and side panes meet shaped pillars and silver rails. The aero blades have depth; wheel pivots and vehicle handling configuration remain unchanged. Existing livery and weathering systems remain in use.

The prepared Electric meshes, racing shadow proxies, Garage template and Electric preview pictures were regenerated from the source. The prepared regression checks source hashes and actual resource paths, and an independent same-process comparison found no surface-array differences across 453 full/simple mesh instances.

Validation on the final source: procedural redesign 149/149, prepared redesign 150/150, door shape 100/100, actual Compatibility Garage/race 58/58 and Super Wash 286/286. The detailed and simple models have 116,096 and 37,085 triangles respectively. The Godot editor import completed; it reported that the Android build-tools directory could not be opened. No Android build or device performance test was performed. Desktop Compatibility and desktop Mobile each captured 18 clean/worn views without capture failures.

All six Garage templates were subsequently regenerated because their editor validity guard tracks shared geometry-source hashes. The Garage template regression passes 24/24 with the actual editable-kit setting used by the Garage. The unchanged historical fixture reports 23/24 because it does not enable the Kart's editable kits; its adapted check is retained at `tmp/volt-garage-prepared-current-kits.gd`. All 37 guarded source hashes remained unchanged during the bake.

The actual [side](evidence/volt-premium-reference-2026-10-30/compatibility/side-opposite-clean.png), [front three-quarter](evidence/volt-premium-reference-2026-10-30/compatibility/front-quarter-high-clean.png), [rear three-quarter](evidence/volt-premium-reference-2026-10-30/compatibility/rear-quarter-clean.png), and [race camera](evidence/volt-premium-reference-2026-10-30/app-compatibility/race.png) were visually inspected. Compared with the target, the side surfacing and wheel detail remain simpler, and the front fascia is more upright. A small shading discontinuity remains near the front fascia/side join. Appearance acceptance remains open.
